1154: SLPI/sensors and Wi-Fi at the same time. The refusal "needs bergamotawlan=0" is gone. (1) The GLINK/QRTR transport takes the edge as a parameter
(ipc_*_e(struct glink_edge *ge, ...), pdm_rx_e, ge_setup_e; bodies unchanged because the parameter is named ge); the modem keeps its
old names as wrappers on the global ge (always &ge_modem now), the SLPI code passes &ge_slpi explicitly. (2) Per-edge ipc_tx staging and
QRTR packet buffers (were static). (3) Locks: SMEM allocator (local mutex around the TCSR hwlock, whose owner id is shared by the whole AP),
AOSS QMP, the SCM assign buffer. (4) The SLPI has its own FAT buffers (struct wl_fat carries fatbuf/dirbuf; fat_mount() = the shared ones, as
before). (5) With Wi-Fi on the SLPI thread waits for the modem (MPSS ready and IPCRTR open, 5 min limit), never replaces the shared QMP/doorbell
mappings, reuses an open QMP link, retries RPMh while the Wi-Fi stage is in it. (6) Keep mode: 10 ms poll while streaming, stats every 10 s for a
minute then every 5 min, sensors parked when nobody reads /dev/bergamota-sensors for 5 s (restarted when a reader returns), and up to 3
restarts after an SLPI crash (stale SMP2P value ignored). Requires 1137-1153.

